.TH SAGE 1 "" "SageMath for Kali" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sage \- mathematical software using the system Python
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sage
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ files ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Start the SageMath interactive interpreter, execute Sage files, or run a command.
The Kali package uses /usr/bin/python3 and Debian's installed mathematics libraries.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "-c " command
Execute Sage code, including Sage's preparsing syntax.
.TP
.BR -python ", " --python
Run /usr/bin/python3, forwarding all following arguments unchanged.
For example: sage -python script.py, or sage -python -c 'import sage.all'.
.TP
.BR -t ", " --test
Run Sage's doctest runner, forwarding all following arguments.
For example: sage -t example.sage. Use sage -t --help for runner options.
.TP
.BR -n ", " --notebook
Start the Jupyter notebook server. Requires sagemath-jupyter.
.TP
.BR -V ", " --version
Print the installed Sage version.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show the options accepted by the installed Sage command-line interface.
.SH NOTES
Other arguments are forwarded to Sage's Python command-line interface.
Python package installation follows Debian's system Python policy; install
packaged dependencies with APT.
